From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Craig <lacraig3@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 22:46:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] panda: main_loop_wait callback at each main-loop iteration

pandare2 runs its queued main-loop work (snap, revert_async, cont) from
this callback; it had no call site.  It runs after main_loop_should_exit()
has acted on stop requests (a vCPU callback stops the VM, then queues the
work), and outside main_loop_wait itself, so savevm/loadvm are not nested
in an aio dispatch.
---
 system/runstate.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/system/runstate.c b/system/runstate.c
index 569841239f1dee0918a65cd85fc2da6f425d6eef..c5becbef907d6b0050fcdc93399cd9b42d0c3927 100644
--- a/system/runstate.c
+++ b/system/runstate.c
@@ -57,6 +57,7 @@
 #include "system/replay.h"
 #include "system/reset.h"
 #include "system/runstate.h"
+#include "panda/hooks.h"
 #include "system/runstate-action.h"
 #include "system/confidential-guest-support.h"
 #include "system/system.h"
@@ -950,6 +951,8 @@ int qemu_main_loop(void)
     int status = EXIT_SUCCESS;
 
     while (!main_loop_should_exit(&status)) {
+        /* after main_loop_should_exit() acted on stop requests */
+        panda_callbacks_main_loop_wait();
         main_loop_wait(false);
     }
 
